Trademarks
----------
Pilot shows other companies' app icons and logos so you can recognise the apps it installs, opens and drives:

- Packaging/catalogue-icons/: the icons of the apps in Install's catalogue.
- Packaging/webapp-icons/: the icons of the sites Install › Web App offers.
- The Claude mark on extension gauges (Sources/Pilot/System/ExtensionGaugeIcon.swift), drawn from CodexBar's path.

These names, icons and logos are trademarks of their owners. They are not covered by Pilot's MIT licence or by
CodexBar's, they are used only to name the app or service they belong to, and their use implies no endorsement by or
affiliation with those owners. A fork that redistributes Pilot is responsible for its own use of them.

Third-party code and assets
---------------------------
- Sources/PilotTiler/ and Sources/PilotTilerPrivateApi/: from AeroSpace (MIT); see the LICENSE in each folder.
- Sources/CGhostty/ghostty.h: Ghostty's embedding header (MIT); see Sources/CGhostty/LICENSE. Scripts/build-ghosttykit.sh
  builds libghostty from Ghostty's own source; what it links is listed in Packaging/Ghostty-THIRD-PARTY.txt.
- Helpers/pilot-files/vendor/cardinal/: Cardinal's search engine (MIT); see its LICENSE and NOTICE.
- Packaging/*-LICENSE.txt and *-NOTICES.txt: the licences of the other libraries, models and data Pilot bundles or
  downloads (CodexBar, gemoji, Omarchy, WhisperKit, FluidAudio, Whisper, Parakeet, Kokoro, Real-ESRGAN).
- Packaging/Fonts/: each face with its own licence beside it.
- The Rust crates of Helpers/pilot-files keep their licences in the cargo registry; Scripts/rust-licenses.py collects
  them into the app.

General › About › Acknowledgements in the app lists the same credits.
